# {{BKIT_MANAGED_MARKER}}

# Worktrees, plan logs, per-run sentinels. Sentinels are written mid-run, read by
# the same run's Failure Path, cleared at next Step 1 — never bookkeeping, so
# path-scoped staging must not commit them.
.worktrees/
docs/plans/*/logs/**/raw/
docs/plans/*/logs/**/.lock
# Per-run sentinels sit in BOOK_PATHS-staged logs — without these lines a Failure
# Path commit captures them and the next `rm -f` shows as a tracked deletion.
docs/plans/*/logs/**/.deferred-blocked
docs/plans/*/logs/**/.rebase-failed

# Repo-global dev critical-section lock (cross-FID)
.bkit/.dev.lock
.bkit/.runtime-cursor

.bkit/.roadmap-shortlist.json
.bkit/.roadmap-reverse-sync.json

# Claude Code /schedule daemon lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Cloud setup docs — `bkit install` inlines resolved .envrc secrets; never commit.
# One per host: .claude/bkit-cloud.md (Claude Code web), .cursor/bkit-cloud.md (Cursor Background Agents)
.claude/bkit-cloud.md
.cursor/bkit-cloud.md

# Claude native worktrees (isolation:worktree / EnterWorktree) — transient full-tree
# copies; ignore or slop:delta double-counts the checkout
.claude/worktrees/

# cursor / opencode — no project-local worktree or runtime dir to ignore.
# Cursor agents run in remote VMs; opencode state lives at ~/.local/share/opencode
# (XDG_DATA_HOME). bkit-managed files in .opencode/ are tracked.

# husky 9 stub (auto-generated by `husky` from prepare)
.husky/_

# Coverage (vitest --coverage) — regenerated each run, never commit
coverage/

# Playwright artifacts — grow under [verbose ci]
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.last-run.json
playwright/.auth/

# Advisories — regenerated by `bkit install` / `check` / `doctor`
.bkit/advisories.md

# Local MCP / agent secrets — never commit
.bkit/.env

# <!-- bkit:end -->
